      "message": "When finished interpolating in premul the values left on the stack should look like the following, where `rgb0`,`a0` is the (initial, unpremultiplied) color at the beginning of a range and `rgb1`,`a1` is the (initial, unpremultiplied) color at the end of the range, and `t` is how far along that range the point is (all values 0 to 1).\n\n```((rgb1*a1-rgb0*a0)*t+rgb0*a0)/((a1-a0)*t+a0)```\n\nThe initial `rgb*a` premuls are done ahead of time. The `rgb` and `a` are interpolated, the `rgb/a` is done and the `a` is discarded (will be provided by the transparency mask shader).",
